Import the C function thrd_create taking a pointer to unsigned long integer and a pointer to function taking pointer to void returning integer and a pointer to void, returning an integer, from the header "threads.h".
Import the C function thrd_join taking an unsigned long integer and a pointer to integer, returning an integer, from the header "threads.h".
Declare counter as atomic integer with value 0.
Procedure worker takes arg as pointer to void returns integer:
    Declare i as integer with value 0.
    Declare previous as integer with value 0.
    While i is less than 1000:
        Set previous to Atomic fetch add 1 to counter.
        Increase i by 1.
    End while.
    Return 0.
End procedure.
Declare a as unsigned long integer.
Declare b as unsigned long integer.
Declare c as unsigned long integer.
Declare status as integer.
Set status to Call thrd_create with Address of a, Address of worker, null pointer done.
Set status to Call thrd_create with Address of b, Address of worker, null pointer done.
Set status to Call thrd_create with Address of c, Address of worker, null pointer done.
Set status to Call thrd_join with a, null pointer done.
Set status to Call thrd_join with b, null pointer done.
Set status to Call thrd_join with c, null pointer done.
Say Atomic load of counter.
